{"title":"2014 Indonesia MO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Is it possible to fill a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d278803d72fcc493afb1559174a483aa7f41d143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> grid with each of the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/5597f6815ed01a3ee6f37c93d05a873cc5135a3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,\\ldots,9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> once each such that the sum of any two numbers sharing a side is prime?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For some positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46ba6ed097cc88ded349bf99eea89817f135f470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"11\" />, the system <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66fdb9c5e5e6dc948181cdf1c67b264e22536bb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y^2 = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174a4f2a4879ccdb721198e8387cc98fff3e1f56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> has exactly one integral solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" />. Determine all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eec521c60534fed80cc321be32e7347f785c145d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-n$\" width=\"48\" height=\"8\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a trapezoid (quadrilateral with one pair of parallel sides) such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/0076b3d6d6e41b8ede92fc6ffb6ecd67014eba16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB &lt; CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Construct the parallelograms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/7/14701a6b220845a03409ab93049a398e7223acf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEDK$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/6/626f772cbea2f87ce4add856d0b792a9807a0bf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BECL$\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> passes through the midpoint of the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef091d889893c7c10e475a93e4ef626ff70aa5ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Determine all polynomials with integral coefficients <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> such that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are the sides of a right-angled triangle, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/f/9cf84350afbe345e6d78356f6c103fd628705475.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(a), P(b), P(c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" /> are also the sides of a right-angled triangle. (Sides of a triangle are necessarily positive. Note that it's not necessary for the order of sides to be preserved; if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is the hypotenuse of the first triangle, it's not necessary that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/c/c4c7e9cd6a8673cb486059ededd03e42714c4787.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> is the hypotenuse of the second triangle, and similar with the others.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A sequence of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/56551a1cd4be3a5d996736e858917416035f3c8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"11\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/b/7bba916ed81f6e5d3724003cb77199dd7687eb88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k + a_l = a_m + a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"13\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/227803fe7417222e20de262d948738bc778bf5f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k,l,m,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/e/8ee6b843af0caf0a16b3389e65992fd510338589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kl = mn$\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" />. Prove that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adf0600eadd15aa783dcc6d2c93d371b56cd8557.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_p \\le a_q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/1/2315f52078440c08de451c4e04086bf0ff12091f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MDA = \\angle ABC$\" width=\"141\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/2117526254eb538b0ddb89322ebcea8dcab8a25d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle NDA = \\angle ACB$\" width=\"137\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcfabd65745f2b759dea1840f9a0753b2f992e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> intersect on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b3402f26b3190aa1f8fae2bb5f456866ba02e82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD^3 = AB \\cdot AC \\cdot AP$\" width=\"171\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/7/2d765491facfe948b0762f128710a8343bdb8794.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k,m,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> are positive integers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/a/8aad1a58d92d1cf1d7cc28a276efb0b1557574b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />. Prove that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/6/546cb4122e733f2ea686fd698c3cde84d142eb50.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{r=0}^m \\dfrac{k \\binom{m}{r} \\binom{n}{k}}{(r+k) \\binom{m+n}{r+k}} = 1\\]\" width=\"166\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A positive integer is called beautiful if it can be represented in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/2/002d828fe2f506ddf378edac1cac988e8050bb63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{x^2+y^2}{x+y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"59\" height=\"42\" /> for two distinct positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />. A positive integer that is not beautiful is ugly.\n</p><p>a) Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/16794ed8d576bcdfc1b48ac2155ce53ff11aff25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2014$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> is a product of a beautiful number and an ugly number.\nb) Prove that the product of two ugly numbers is also ugly.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO\" title=\"2014 Indonesia MO\">2014 Indonesia MO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO\">2013 Indonesia MO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exi